 "en": {
  "name": "Rise of the Ottomans",
  "sub": "1299 – From Söğüt to Bursa",
  "blurb": "After the collapse of the Seljuk Sultanate of Rum, a small frontier beylik rises in Mongol-dominated Anatolia: Osman Bey's Söğüt. Byzantium lies ahead, rival beyliks on every side, the shadow of the Ilkhanate behind. Can a small border chief found a world empire?",
  "setup_intro": "1299: the Seljuk sultanate is dying and the Ilkhanate rules Anatolia through governors. Osman, frontier bey of Söğüt, wants to enlarge his small lands by raids and holy war; ahead lie the Byzantine fortresses of Bithynia and the rivalry of neighbouring beyliks.",
  "events": {
   "0": "Ghazan Khan defeats the Mamluks in Syria; Damascus falls to the Ilkhanate.",
   "1": "Battle of Bapheus: Osman Bey crushes the Byzantine army; the gates of Bithynia open.",
   "2": "Battle of Shaqhab: the Mamluks finally halt the Ilkhanid advance into Syria.",
   "3": "King Philip IV of France has the Knights Templar arrested.",
   "4": "The Seljuk Sultanate of Rum effectively ends; Anatolia is divided between beyliks and Ilkhanid governors.",
   "5": "The Knights Hospitaller seize Rhodes.",
   "6": "Sultan Alauddin Khalji of Delhi dies; the sultanate begins to tremble.",
   "7": "Osman Gazi dies; his son Orhan Bey succeeds him.",
   "8": "Orhan Bey conquers Bursa; the Ottomans gain their first great capital.",
   "9": "Nicaea surrenders; the heart of Bithynia passes to the Ottomans."
  },
  "objectives": {
